      "## Immediate danger and the reporting duty can coexist",
      "A report to a protective-services agency is not always an emergency rescue response. If a child or vulnerable adult is in immediate danger, the counselor may also need emergency services, law enforcement, medical evaluation, a safe caregiver, or another action permitted or required by law. Conversely, an emergency response does not automatically replace a required statutory report.",
      "Ask two separate questions:",
      "1. **What must happen now to reduce immediate danger?**\n2. **What report does the statute require, to whom, and by when?**",
      "## Institutional procedures and personal responsibility",
      "An agency may instruct counselors to inform a supervisor, risk manager, or designated reporting lead. Follow lawful procedures, but verify whether the statute imposes a direct duty. In some jurisdictions, internal notification supplements rather than replaces a report to the authorized government recipient.",
